        "ai_gen_block_41479e3_yyzcqt": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_41479e3",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "",
            "heading_size": 28,
            "desktop_cards": "5",
            "mobile_cards": "1.2",
            "card_background": "#ffffff",
            "border_color": "#ececec",
            "corner_radius": 14,
            "star_color": "#c9a26d",
            "show_arrows": true,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "review_1_photo": "shopify://shop_images/5leg.webp",
            "review_1_name": "Elena B.",
            "review_1_rating": "5",
            "review_1_title": "5 stars · 1.75 m · Take size L",
            "review_1_text": "Lovely tights, good quality, and really warm. HOWEVER:\n\nI am 1.75 meters tall and weigh 65kg, I usually wear size M. I got a size M and they run a little short: the waist sits where it should, but they feel slightly tight on my long legs. If you are as tall as me, take size L.\n\nAside from that: a lovely skin-like finish, they hold the tummy in well, and they didn't tear even when my cat sank his claws into them (I swear!).\n\nI'm reordering in size L and they'll be perfect. I just wanted to warn tall girls.",
            "review_2_photo": "shopify://shop_images/leg8.jpg",
            "review_2_name": "Chiara L.",
            "review_2_rating": "5",
            "review_2_title": "5 stars · Thigh chafing solved",
            "review_2_text": "I have always had the problem of thighs rubbing together, and in winter with regular skirts and tights, it was a nightmare. Either they would tear immediately, or I had to always wear shorts underneath (which were then visible).\n\nThese are like magic: durable fabric with no friction, zero inner thigh chafing, and above all, THEY DO NOT TEAR. I've been using them since September and they are still like new.\n\nThe high waistband is comfortable, it doesn't roll down like that of regular tights. And no one notices that my legs aren't bare, I swear! Super natural effect.\n\nThe only downside, if I really have to find one: they take a little longer to put on than thin tights, but it's totally worth it.",
            "review_3_photo": "shopify://shop_images/3leg.webp",
            "review_3_name": "Martina P.",
            "review_3_rating": "5",
            "review_3_title": "5 stars · Size L · After pregnancy",
            "review_3_text": "After pregnancy, I had a belly that I didn't like at all. I tried separate shapewear but they were very uncomfortable under clothes.\n\nThese are like 2 in 1: they look like regular tights but have this high waistband that keeps everything in place. No one notices that I'm wearing them; they look like real skin.\n\nI took size L (I'm 1.68 m and 72 kg after giving birth) and they fit perfectly. They don't squeeze too much but they also don't create wrinkles.\n\nOh, little tip: wash them by hand or on a delicate cycle in the washing machine; I washed them at 40°C the first time and they shrank a bit, but nothing serious.",
            "review_4_photo": "shopify://shop_images/4leg_40e61840-818f-413c-b582-4a113a2a7ef2.webp",
            "review_4_name": "Alessia T.",
            "review_4_rating": "5",
            "review_4_title": "5 stars · ZERO issues test",
            "review_4_text": "Okay, this is the thing that stressed me the most with regular tights... every time I bent down, I was afraid everything would show 💀\n\nWith these, ZERO problems. I tested them in every possible way (yes, I even took mirror selfies while bent over lol) and you can't see ANYTHING. They're just the right thickness.\n\nAnd anyway, girls, they are super warm. I even use them to ride my bike to work and I don't feel cold. Before, I always had to wear pants.\n\nThe only note: the feet are not lined, so if your feet get cold, still wear socks under your boots. But in my opinion, it's better this way because I don't sweat.",
            "review_5_photo": "shopify://shop_images/2leg.webp",
            "review_5_name": "Giulia R.",
            "review_5_rating": "5",
            "review_5_title": "5 stars · Size M/L",
            "review_5_text": "Ok I have to be honest. I bought them just because my legs were cold under skirts in winter. I didn't expect them to make my butt look this good too lol 😂\n\nThat single seam really makes a difference, zero diaper effect like my old thermal leggings. And they keep you warm for real, I wore them at -3°C and I felt great.\n\nMy only \"problem\": now I want to go out in a skirt all the time even when it's cold haha"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
